    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_f87a1bc3",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: trump_meme_2011_2016; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts Donald Trump speaking, with overlaid text claiming he said in 2011, \"all americans are idiots,\" and that \"in 2016 they proved it.\" This meme is harmful because it falsely attributes a specific, derogatory statement to Trump and then uses the 2016 election outcome as a supposed \"proof\" of its truth. The intent is to discredit Trump by implying his own words were validated by voters, which is a misleading and potentially inflammatory narrative. The meme relies on a false equivalence and misrepresentation of political discourse, potentially inciting division or reinforcing negative stereotypes about voters or political opponents. It does not target specific protected groups but uses a generalized, derogatory statement about 'all Americans' to create a divisive and potentially toxic message.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_c178f2cf"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
