      "label": "Divisive Narrative",
      "description": "The meme constructs a divisive narrative by implying that Trump's false statement was 'proved' by voters in 2016. This narrative is harmful because it suggests that voters are unintelligent or complicit in their own political defeat, which can incite anger and reinforce negative stereotypes about political opponents.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_c178f2cf"
